{
  "format": 1,
  "notes": [
    "WHAT GROWS WHERE. One entry per species (the ids of tree_trunk_presets.json and plant_presets.json). The vegetation system reads this file once, turns it into the species table of the C++ scatter (vegi_common.cpp: VG_SP_*) and decides, for every place of the world, which species grow there. A species that is not in this file is never planted.",
    "The climate is the biome pass's own, the 4 + 4 bits of the vegetation map's alpha: temperature 0 (ice) .. 1 (hot), humidity 0 (dry) .. 1 (wet). Reading the biome table of game2.js: ice t < 0.15, boreal 0.15 .. 0.35 (tundra m < 0.35, taiga m > 0.35), cool 0.3 .. 0.55 (shrubland m 0.1 .. 0.3, woodland 0.3 .. 0.55, temperate forest 0.55 .. 0.8), warm 0.5 .. 0.75 (desert m < 0.1, savanna 0.1 .. 0.3, grassland 0.25 .. 0.45, woodland, forest, rainforest m > 0.72), tropical t > 0.65 (savanna, forest 0.4 .. 0.6, jungle m > 0.6). The temperature already falls with the height (the biome pass takes 0.7 of the map's height off it).",
    "temperature / humidity: [lo, hi] the species grows inside (it still grows `soft` past them, thinning: the defaults' soft). altitude: [lo, hi] as a FRACTION of the land's height (0 = the sea's level, 1 = the highest peak: the same for a small world and a large one; in game2 the land is 600 m high, the snow line is at 0.55 .. 0.7, bare rock from 0.45). slope: the steepest ground it stands on (rise over run, 1 = 45 degrees). weight: how common it is among the others that suit the place (1 = a main species). scale: [lo, hi] the size of an individual (1 = the preset's size). stand: the size in metres of its groves (0 = it is mixed in everywhere it grows).",
    "trees: role 'canopy' is drawn from the map's TREE density (red), role 'under' (small trees: the understory, hedges, orchard trees) from its BUSH density (green). plants: driver 'grass' (the map's grass density, blue), 'bush' (green) or 'tree' (red: a plant of the forest floor, around trunks). density: tufts per square metre where the driver is 1. patch: 'noise' (a patch about 25 m wide, salt picks which) or 'sin' (a lattice of patches) = the plant grows in patches of its own, 'near_tree' = around the trunks of the cell. enabled false = left out (the crops and garden plants: a field or a garden is a place of its own, not a biome).",
    "variation: what the PLACE does to an individual (the scatter, once; 0 = nothing, 1 = the full effect, up to 2). crowd: where the map's density is high the tree is taller and narrower, alone in the open it is broader. site: a place that suits it less (past its climate or height limits, or steep) makes it smaller, down to about half. age: stands of age_size metres are young (smaller, narrower) or old (bigger, broader). It acts on top of `scale`. Set in defaults.tree and overridden by one species; leave it out of defaults and a species is only as varied as its scale range and the shader's own spread (config: var_width, var_lean, var_color, var_stand).",
    "A species is chosen with weight x climate fit x ground fit (and its groves); the place is only as dense as the best sum of fits (a poor place has fewer plants). The library has few tropical trees: the jungle is oaks, jacarandas, palms and eucalypts until more species are added here."
  ],
